WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.117
Semicolons and Colons

00:00:02.497 --> 00:00:06.548
Semicolon = period. Colon = here’s what I mean.

00:00:07.748 --> 00:00:08.747
How to spot it

00:00:09.147 --> 00:00:11.506
Semicolons and colons in the choices

00:00:12.056 --> 00:00:13.680
A blank between two parts

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:18.319
It’s testing: the exact job of each punctuation mark

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.314
The method

00:00:20.714 --> 00:00:24.237
Step 1: Semicolon? Test both sides

00:00:24.517 --> 00:00:26.269
Each must be a full sentence.

00:00:26.819 --> 00:00:30.074
Step 2: Colon? Test the left side

00:00:30.354 --> 00:00:31.987
It must be a full sentence.

00:00:32.537 --> 00:00:35.301
Step 3: Does the right side explain?

00:00:35.581 --> 00:00:38.853
A list, example or explanation fits a colon.

00:00:39.403 --> 00:00:41.755
Step 4: Never after a verb

00:00:42.035 --> 00:00:44.465
“The ingredients are:” is wrong.

00:00:45.015 --> 00:00:46.125
In a few words

00:00:46.275 --> 00:00:50.386
Semicolon: both sides. Colon: left side.

00:00:51.586 --> 00:00:52.409
The rules

00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:54.347
Semicolon = period

00:00:54.627 --> 00:00:58.250
Wrong: The lab was quiet; because everyone left.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.907
Right: The lab was quiet; everyone had left.

00:01:02.457 --> 00:01:04.459
Colon needs a full sentence first

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:08.325
Wrong: The ingredients are: flour and eggs.

00:01:08.605 --> 00:01:11.255
Right: She had one goal: winning.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:15.039
After a colon: explain, list, show

00:01:15.319 --> 00:01:18.983
Right: The cause was clear: the battery overheated.

00:01:19.533 --> 00:01:21.853
Semicolons split lists that have commas

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:27.679
Right: Nairobi, Kenya; Lima, Peru; and Hanoi, Vietnam

00:01:28.879 --> 00:01:29.920
Let’s try one

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.851
The ship’s log revealed the cause of the delay ______ a storm had forced the crew to shelter in a

00:01:35.851 --> 00:01:37.292
harbor for six days.

00:01:37.942 --> 00:01:43.652
Left side: the ship’s log revealed the cause of the delay. That’s a full sentence.

00:01:44.202 --> 00:01:46.594
The right side explains what the cause was.

00:01:47.157 --> 00:01:50.602
A comma makes a splice. Nothing makes a run-on.

00:01:50.602 --> 00:01:55.517
And loses the link. A colon introduces the explanation.

00:01:55.517 --> 00:01:56.732
Choice B.

00:01:57.932 --> 00:01:58.927
Common traps

00:01:59.327 --> 00:02:00.628
Colon after a verb

00:02:00.908 --> 00:02:05.136
“includes:” or “are:” leaves the left side incomplete.

00:02:05.686 --> 00:02:07.480
Semicolon before a fragment

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.577
Both sides must stand alone.

00:02:10.777 --> 00:02:12.294
Semicolons and Colons

00:02:12.574 --> 00:02:16.685
Semicolon: both sides. Colon: left side.

00:02:17.235 --> 00:02:18.008
Spot it

00:02:18.208 --> 00:02:20.567
Semicolons and colons in the choices

00:02:21.117 --> 00:02:21.824
Steps

00:02:22.024 --> 00:02:25.888
1. Semicolon: both sides full sentences

00:02:26.168 --> 00:02:29.383
2. Colon: left side a full sentence

00:02:29.663 --> 00:02:33.391
3. Right side explains or lists? → colon

00:02:33.671 --> 00:02:36.302
4. Never a colon right after a verb

00:02:36.852 --> 00:02:37.605
Remember

00:02:37.805 --> 00:02:39.343
Semicolon = period

00:02:39.623 --> 00:02:41.813
Colon needs a full sentence before it

00:02:42.093 --> 00:02:45.968
After a colon: explanation, list, example

00:02:46.248 --> 00:02:49.019
Semicolons split list items that have commas

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:50.174
Trap

00:02:50.374 --> 00:02:52.378
Colon after a verb or “such as”

00:02:53.128 --> 00:02:56.823
